When using libraries such as Angular 19 and frameng, make you sure have sufficient knowledge of that version you are using. If not, search its documentation and make sure you fully understand that version before proceeding. 
For example when working on Angular templates, don't use deprecated syntax like the control flow (*ngIf), use new practices introduced in Angular 19 (@if). 

Try to build all UI components with PrimeNG, if the library doesn't have suitable components, build your own. 

Never use `any` in types, fix them. Also run `bun run build` to confirm your code works.

When working in the Angular app and calling a backend service, is the service is not created yet, make assumptions with placeholders. 
Don't hard code any dynamic data in the UI, you can mock service responses, while the Angular components should be feature-complete. 

Follow best practices for project strucure. Don't embed HTML and SCSS into TS files, separate them into their own files. 

If you failed to update any files (writing error), delete the file then create with original content plus your changes.

Be DRY with SCSS code. Always search and reuse shared styles before writing new styles.

When working with user interface, make sure all text/copy support translation. Add translations for new text to all supported languages. 
